Assertions:
[NAV] the header 'Cart' link points directly to /cart — no mini-cart overlay exists in this theme {OBSERVED}
[DOM] each '.vc-line-item' row is present with product image, product name, unit price, quantity input and line total {OBSERVED}
[NAV] URL is {{FRONT_URL}}/cart after clicking the header 'Cart' link {OBSERVED}
[FORMAT] prices formatted to 2 decimal places {OBSERVED}

[STATE] displayed quantity is rejected or reverted to the last valid value 1, not -1 {BL} {OBSERVED} (per BL-CART-001; 2026-07-27 trace shows the changeCartItemsQuantity response carries validationErrors[PRODUCT_MIN_QTY] yet still echoes items[0].quantity=-1, and the storefront currently binds the spinbutton directly to that echoed value — this assertion is expected to legitimately FAIL until the echo is fixed)
[MATH] line total = unit price × 1 and subtotal = sum of all line totals at quantity 1 (2 decimal places) — no mismatch between a rejected/reverted displayed quantity and the computed money fields {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a generic transport-error banner/toast renders in the Order Summary after the rejected -1 attempt {OBSERVED} (2026-08-05) — the app's global server-error handler, not a cart-specific validation message; the echoed -1 defect itself is unchanged
[STATE] no JavaScript console errors are thrown after the attempt {OBSERVED}

[STATE] the native number-input constraint blocks the non-numeric characters from being entered at all - displayed quantity remains 1 {OBSERVED} (browser-native input type=number behavior, not app-level validation; this assertion is expected to PASS)
[STATE] cart totals remain unchanged (quantity stayed at 1 throughout the attempt) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] no cart error banner is rendered for the blocked abc attempt - element absent from DOM {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no JavaScript console errors are thrown after the attempt {OBSERVED}

Cross_Layer_Checks:
[API] no changeCartItemsQuantity mutation is sent at all for this non-numeric input — the client-rejected value never reaches the server, so there is no GraphQL response to check for a top-level errors[] entry
[CONSOLE] no JS errors after the non-numeric keyboard-entry attempt
[NETWORK] no API call is triggered at all - the native input constraint blocks the character before any request is attempted {OBSERVED}

[API] the decimal quantity is expected to be rejected or rounded client-side before any mutation is sent, so no GraphQL errors[] should come back; today's defect instead sends 1.5 verbatim and the failure surfaces as the transport-level HTTP 400 tracked by the [NETWORK] check below, not as a GraphQL errors[] entry
[CONSOLE] no JS errors after the decimal-quantity keyboard-entry attempt
[NETWORK] no failed (4xx/5xx) API calls are triggered by client-side-rejected input - the client must validate/round the value before submitting to changeCartItemsQuantity {OBSERVED: currently fails - 2026-07-27 trace shows quantity 1.5 sent verbatim, producing HTTP 400 Unable-to-convert-to-Int}

